IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sge-p10a-363`

-- Tests of s 363 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: pre-existing charges). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the
-- assertion, before the run. The company is registered on 1 March 2027; 30 days after that is 31 March 2027.

§ `Section 363(1): the statement of a pre-existing charge`

-- Arguments: the charge existed before registration; it would have needed registering under Division 8 of Part 4.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Either limb of the "if" missing: no statement is required for it (read as the text's no).
#ASSERT `s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 363(1) the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 31 3 2027

-- Arguments: date of registration; a statement has been lodged; in the prescribed manner with the prescribed particulars; the date lodged; the date asked.
-- Lodged on the last day, in the prescribed manner: in time.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Lodged well inside the period.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Lodged the day after the last day: too late.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lodged in time but not in the prescribed manner, or without the prescribed particulars: not what the subsection requires.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Nothing lodged: on the last day the period still runs; the day after, the duty has been missed.
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 31 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a rule: 30 days from the date of registration (AT 0). Lodged on day 30: in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 363(1) the company must lodge a statement of a pre-existing charge within 30 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 363(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge` AT 30

-- Nothing lodged and the clock reaches day 31: the 30 days have run out, so breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 363(1) the company must lodge a statement of a pre-existing charge within 30 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

-- Lodged on day 31: too late, so breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 363(1) the company must lodge a statement of a pre-existing charge within 30 days after the date of registration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 363(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge` AT 31

§ `Section 363(2): who may lodge`

#ASSERT `s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither the company nor a person interested: the text grants nothing and says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363(3): recovering the fees`

#ASSERT `s 363(3) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The company itself effected the registration: the "Where" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 363(3) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The amount is "the amount of any fees properly paid": here 250 dollars.
#ASSERT `s 363(3) the amount of fees the person is entitled to recover from the company` TRUE 250 EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `s 363(3) the amount of fees the person is entitled to recover from the company` FALSE 250 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363(4): default and the offence`

-- Arguments: default is made in complying with (1); the person is the company; the person is an officer who is in default.
-- Default made: the company and every officer in default are each guilty.
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An officer who is not in default: the subsection reaches only "every officer of the company who is in default".
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No default: the "if" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty".
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 363(4) penalty` OF 1000, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 363(4) penalty` OF 1000, TRUE)
-- Not guilty: the subsection states no penalty for the person.
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363(5): a failure does not affect the charge`

-- Arguments: there has been a failure to comply with (1); the thing of the charge.
#ASSERT `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` TRUE `s 363(5) a security of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` TRUE `s 363(5) a right of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` TRUE `s 363(5) a priority of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` TRUE `s 363(5) an obligation of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No failure: nothing for the subsection to say.
#ASSERT `s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` FALSE `s 363(5) a security of the charge` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363(6): the Court's relief`

-- Arguments: satisfied (a1) accidental or other sufficient cause; satisfied (a2) not prejudicial; satisfied (b) just and equitable on other grounds;
-- the application is by the company; by a person interested.
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not satisfied of any ground: "on being satisfied" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Satisfied, but nobody entitled has applied: "on the application of the company or any person interested" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Terms and conditions: the one the text names, or one the Court thinks just and expedient.
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363(7): sections 134, 135, 136 and 138 apply`

-- Arguments: the charge is required to be lodged under (1); the section.
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) section 134` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) section 135` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) section 136` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) section 138` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Section 137, say: not named, so the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) another section` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A charge that is not required to be lodged under (1): not covered.
#ASSERT `s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` FALSE `s 363(7) section 134` EQUALS NOTHING
